Z||000000||BN Boomer||07-18-2000||11:28 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/boomers_railroad_files/steam1.jpg"> <P>That kind of puts things into perspective, huh?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>The railroad I am employed by, namely the Burlington Northern Santa Fe, recently ran what was known as the Employee Appreciation Special 2000 through the region I work in. The train consists of the historic Southern Pacific X4449 steam locomotive, it's 2 tenders, the BNSF 4449 GE Dash 9-44CW diesel locomotive, a tool car, a generator car, and a combination of 12 sleeper and coach cars. I chose to ride it along with my family from Skykomish, WA to Wenatchee, WA via Steven's Pass and through the 8 mile long Cascade Tunnel. I've never been much of a fan of steam locomotives before, but this thing sure made an impression on me. The thing is huge. The driving wheels are about as tall as myself, around 6 feet. I had a chance to tour the locomotive cab while it was sitting in the switchyard where I was working the night before I rode it. Simply awesome. I loved watching it pull into Skykomish belching steam and smoke. You wouldn't believe the number of railfans who showed up to photograph this thing, pace it alongside US 2 over the pass to photograph/film it, or keep getting ahead of it to take more pictures. We passed some of the same people 4 or 5 times. There was even a film crew following us in a helicopter. The weather was absolutely perfect, too. What a great day. My family was thrilled throughout the 4 hour trip. All in all, 2 big thumbs up from Boomer.<P>Here's a couple of more pics of it sitting in Delta Yard as the sun is coming up over the Cascades.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/boomers_railroad_files/steam3.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/boomers_railroad_files/steam2.jpg"> <P>Here's the executive coach car, the Fox River, that my family and I rode in. We were on the upper level. Very nice.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/boomers_railroad_files/steam4.jpg"> <P>I don't know if there are any railfans around here or not, but I hope you guys enjoyed the pics!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||14
